                <note rend="inline" type="source">211.62/82: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Germany</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Sackett</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-07-10T19:00:00-04:00">July 10, 1930—7
                    p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>68. Your No. 79, July 8, 4 p.m. President’s full power signed July 9 authorizing
                    you to sign extradition treaty shown German Embassy, Washington, which will
                    advise German Government by cable of its satisfactory character. Proceed to
                    signature. Full power will be mailed first opportunity for delivery by you to
                    Foreign Office.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
